h z = z * Normal
main = h 0.0
-- The helper-extraction rewrite of arithmetic/drawBoundZeroTimesNormal. A zero
-- factor is the absorbing element only when it is statically zero at the
-- product (`isStaticZero`: a literal, or a {0} value-set tag); inside `h` it
-- is a parameter, so the product is inverted through a division by it: the
-- answer is NaN at dim 1 at every point (verified on branch
-- fuzz-admission-oracle-bugs, and identically at dev 9ca6755). Task helper-parameter-zero-factor-answers-nan.
